/*
  VehicleHeader.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 feature view · 0301 · VehicleHeader (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native
  `VehicleHeader` resolves (table "VehicleHeader") lives here with its web
  `t(key, default)` English value. These entries fold into the app
  `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept in a
  per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings without
  editing the shared catalog.

  The first group is the exact key extracted from the web source
  (features/vehicles/components/vehicle-detail/VehicleHeader.tsx). The second group is
  the status-label map (web types/fsm/vehicle.ts VEHICLE_STATE_LABELS), resolved here
  because the web Badge prints the raw status token while native shows the project's
  canonical localizable label. The third group backs the native chrome: the back /
  VIN / empty / error / freshness copy, so the Swift sources hold no English literals.
*/

/* --- Key from the web source (parity) --- */
